  "result": "`Cart.remove('sku-1')` now removes the Widget line, and the tests pass.\n\n**Root cause:** in `shop/models.py:33`, `Cart.remove` filtered lines on `l.item.name != sku`. It compared the SKU you passed in against each item's display name (`'Widget'`). Those never match, so no line was ever removed.\n\n**Fix:** the filter now uses `l.item.sku != sku`, which matches how `Cart.add` identifies lines.\n\n**Checks:**\n- `shop/demo.py` now prints `1`, meaning only the Gadget line is left. Before the fix it would have printed 2.\n- All 6 tests pass. I ran them with `python3 -m unittest discover` because pytest isn't installed here.\n\nNone of the existing tests call `Cart.remove`, which is how this bug got through. I can add a regression test for it if you'd like.",
